{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And it shall be</b> — Yefet says: the coastal region, the name of the city is there upon, and it shall be Not Kerot, shepherds who cut for themselves."], :book :zephaniah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The Hebrew is compressed and syntactically opaque; translated hyper-literally. 'Not Kerot' (נות כרות) is Ibn Ezra's citation of Yefet's reading of the place name; the trailing relative clause 'shepherds who cut for themselves' is Yefet's etymology."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zephaniah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zfanya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:47:19.387995049Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}